# Pattern matching for `instanceof`

## Test, cast, use → one step

```java
// before
if (obj instanceof String) {
    String s = (String) obj;
    System.out.println(s.length());
}
// after — a type pattern binds when the test passes
if (obj instanceof String s) {
    System.out.println(s.length());   // s already a String
}
```

Type name once; check & cast can't disagree.

## Flow scoping — `s` lives where the match is proven

```java
if (obj instanceof String s && s.length() > 3) { ... }   // ✅ safe after &&

if (!(obj instanceof String s)) return;
s.length();                                              // ✅ reaching here proves it
```

## Reach for it wisely

- Great for **boundaries** — parsing, interop, `equals`
- A ladder of `instanceof`? Prefer **polymorphism** or a **sealed `switch`**
- Same type pattern powers `switch` & record patterns (next)
